ralph/progress.txt:19642:- Remaining risks / follow-ups: BE-0277 (Implement POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/retry) and BE-0278 (contract tests) still pending — the engine pin here is the authoritative contract until they land. The wire 404-vs-403 distinction for cross-tenant or unknown {job_id} (treat foreign-tenant or unknown-row {job_id} as not-found for non-Support roles, and ALSO not-found for Support because mutating cross-tenant must go through admin break-glass tooling, not the customer-facing retry verb) lives in the contract test for BE-0278 and is intentionally not pinned at the engine layer. Similarly, the job-state precondition (cannot retry a row already in a terminal succeeded state, can retry from failed/cancelled per the worker's idempotency contract) is a service-layer guard, not a policy-engine guard, and is pinned in the BE-0277 service-level tests when they land.
ralph/progress.txt:19855:  - **Engine-only policy-matrix file pattern for CapSupport actions (BE-0285, applicable to BE-0288 admin.import, BE-0291 admin.read, BE-0294 admin.break_glass when those stories land):** Same structural shape as the BE-0282 (job.cancel) CapDeploy template, but with three load-bearing flips:
ralph/progress.txt:19859:  - **Resource Kind for admin actions = KindOrganization (org-rooted), not a deeper KindJob/KindDeployment.** admin.reconcile/import/read/break_glass operate on the source-of-truth view of an entire organization (no parent project, env, or service), so the resource has only Scope.OrganizationID pinned. The grant-containment tests therefore prove that project/env/service-scoped grants deny via ReasonDeniedOutOfScope (one-way covers()), never ReasonAllowedByGrant — admin actions are unreachable through any scoped grant other than org-level Support.
ralph/progress.txt:19881:  - The sibling admin endpoints in the same P=1 batch (BE-0291 admin.import POST, BE-0294 admin.read dokploy-refs, BE-0297/BE-0300 admin.break_glass) can clone this template by s/AdminReconcileEndpoint/AdminImport|AdminRead|AdminBreakGlass/, swapping ActionAdminReconcile -> ActionAdminImport / ActionAdminRead / ActionAdminBreakGlass; all are CapSupport so the per-role verdict matrix is byte-identical.
ralph/progress.txt:19912:  - The CapSupport admin-action engine-pin template now has THREE instantiations (BE-0285 admin.reconcile, BE-0288 admin.reconcile endpoint-pinned twin, BE-0291 admin.import). The two remaining P=1 batch members in this template family — BE-0294 (admin.read for GET /v1/admin/organizations/{org_id}/dokploy-refs) and BE-0297/BE-0300 (admin.break_glass) — can clone this file with s/AdminImport/AdminRead|AdminBreakGlass/, swapping ActionAdminImport -> ActionAdminRead / ActionAdminBreakGlass and updating the resource framing for the actions' semantics. Per-role verdict matrix stays byte-identical because all four actions are CapSupport.
ralph/progress.txt:19944:  - The CapSupport admin-action engine-pin template now has FOUR instantiations (BE-0285 admin.reconcile, BE-0288 admin.reconcile endpoint-pinned twin, BE-0291 admin.import, BE-0294 admin.read). The two remaining P=1 batch members in this template family — BE-0297 (admin.break_glass POST /v1/admin/break-glass) and BE-0300 (admin.break_glass DELETE /v1/admin/break-glass/{session_id}) — can clone this file with s/AdminRead/AdminBreakGlass/, swapping ActionAdminRead -> ActionAdminBreakGlass and reframing the docstring around session-creation / session-revocation semantics. Per-role verdict matrix stays byte-identical because admin.break_glass is also CapSupport.
ralph/progress.txt:19953:  - Engine-level policy-matrix coverage for action admin.break_glass (POST /v1/admin/break-glass) at internal/controlplane/policy/admin_break_glass_policy_test.go. Structural clone of the BE-0294 (admin.read) template — the action-level engine-pin pattern for CapSupport admin actions whose wire endpoint has not landed yet. Eight Test functions, 30 subtests, all parallel.
ralph/progress.txt:19955:    - Role matrix at home org (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyMatrixRoles): 5 roles (Owner/Admin/Developer/CI/Viewer) deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability, RoleSupport allows ReasonAllowedByRole — the canonical CapSupport one-row-allow shape, photo-negative of CapRead (5/6 allow).
ralph/progress.txt:19956:    - Disabled-principal short-circuit (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyRevokedAndExpiredKeys): underlying role is RoleSupport (would otherwise allow), Disabled=true forces ReasonDeniedPrincipalDisabled for both "revoked key" and "expired key" cases.
ralph/progress.txt:19957:    - Cross-tenant boundary (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyWrongOrganizationPrincipal): Support principal of orgA against orgB allows via ReasonAllowedBySupport (CapSupport is inside the engine's cross-tenant exception clause); every other built-in role denies ReasonDeniedCrossTenant.
ralph/progress.txt:19958:    - Project-grant containment (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyProjectGrantContainment): project-Support on target project denies OutOfScope (one-way covers()); project-Support on sibling project denies OutOfScope; project-Admin denies NoCapability (Admin lacks CapSupport).
ralph/progress.txt:19959:    - Environment-grant containment (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyEnvironmentGrantContainment): env-staging Support denies OutOfScope; env-production Support denies OutOfScope (the AC-symmetric pin); staging-Admin -> production env.write denies (defence-in-depth); env-production Admin denies NoCapability.
ralph/progress.txt:19960:    - Service-grant containment (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyServiceGrantContainment): svc-scoped Support denies OutOfScope on org root; svc Admin denies parent env.write, sibling svc.update, and admin.break_glass NoCapability.
ralph/progress.txt:19961:    - Org-grant capability matrix (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyOrgGrantCapabilityMatrix): Support@org ALLOWS (ReasonAllowedByGrant); Owner/Admin/Developer/Viewer/CI@org all deny NoCapability — Owner is the load-bearing row.
ralph/progress.txt:19962:    - Foreign-home-org "stolen scoped key" guard (TestAdminBreakGlassPolicyForeignHomeOrgGrant): principal home=orgB, foreign grant Support@orgA, resource=orgB -> grant filter drops the grant, verdict ReasonDeniedNoCapability. Pins that CapSupport's cross-tenant exception is gated on the PRINCIPAL'S role caps, never on a grant's role caps.
ralph/progress.txt:19964:  - internal/controlplane/policy/admin_break_glass_policy_test.go: NEW; 8 test functions + 30 subtests; uses shared test-package helpers orgA/orgB/principalIn/assertDecision from policy_test.go; ActionAdminBreakGlass already catalogued as CapSupport at internal/controlplane/policy/catalog.go:134; canonical project ids prj_admin_break_glass_matrix_alpha / prj_admin_break_glass_matrix_beta + break_glass-suffixed ServiceAccount IDs keep the file state-independent from BE-0285's admin_reconcile_policy_test.go fixtures, BE-0288's admin_dokploy_reconcile_endpoint_policy_test.go fixtures, BE-0291's admin_import_policy_test.go fixtures, and BE-0294's admin_read_policy_test.go fixtures, so a future shared helper cannot accidentally couple admin-action matrices.
ralph/progress.txt:19971:  - go test -count=1 -run 'TestAdminBreakGlassPolicy' ./internal/controlplane/policy/ -> ok (0.492s), all 30 subtests PASS
ralph/progress.txt:19976:  - Wire endpoint POST /v1/admin/break-glass, its OpenAPI entry, contract tests, the break-glass session model + lifecycle (TTL, audit-trail, automatic revocation), and the support-audit cross-tenant invariant remain to be implemented in future stories. The engine pin here is the structural barrier protecting the authorization contract until then.
ralph/progress.txt:19977:  - The four admin-action engine pins (admin.reconcile @ BE-0285, admin.import @ BE-0291, admin.read @ BE-0294, admin.break_glass @ BE-0297) now exhaustively pin every CapSupport action in catalog.go. A future catalog row that adds a fifth CapSupport action will need its own engine-pin file under the same template; nothing in the existing four files would catch the gap. The catalog rows themselves (catalog.go:131-134) are unchanged; this story pins the row, not adds it.
ralph/progress.txt:19978:  - BE-0300 (DELETE /v1/admin/break-glass/{session_id}) shares the same action constant ActionAdminBreakGlass, so the next iteration is the endpoint-pinned twin of THIS file — same template as BE-0288's relationship to BE-0285 (admin.reconcile drift listing + reconcile mutation share ActionAdminReconcile). That twin will reuse the canonicalAdminBreakGlassEnd* renamed canonical ids per the BE-0288 distinguishing-suffix rule.
ralph/progress.txt:19980:  - **BE-0297 closes out the CapSupport admin-action engine-pin sweep.** The four CapSupport actions catalogued at internal/controlplane/policy/catalog.go:131-134 (admin.read/import/reconcile/break_glass) now each have a dedicated engine-only policy-matrix file with state-independent canonical ids. The structural template is fully proven across four sibling actions; any future CapSupport admin action MUST follow the same eight-function shape (Roles / Revoked&Expired / WrongOrg / Project / Env / Service / OrgGrant / ForeignHomeOrg) with the canonical-id suffix rule and action-distinct ServiceAccount IDs.
ralph/progress.txt:19981:  - **Mutating-verb framing for CapSupport actions:** admin.break_glass is a mutating verb (creates an elevated session) and admin.reconcile is a mutating verb (issues Dokploy writes), but BOTH are catalogued as CapSupport because the CAPABILITY captures "actions only Yalla support should be able to perform across the tenant boundary" — not "read vs write". The engine's cross-tenant exception (`required == CapRead || CapSupport`) deliberately admits CapSupport regardless of read/write nature. This is the load-bearing distinction from CapDeploy verbs (job.retry, job.cancel) where Support is denied cross-tenant. When a future admin verb lands (e.g. admin.rotate_root_credentials, admin.purge_orphan_dokploy), the question to ask is "does Yalla support need to be able to do this cross-tenant during incident response?" — if yes, CapSupport; if no (e.g. admin actions that should remain inside the tenant's own Owner authority), a different cap class.
ralph/progress.txt:19983:  - **The "single-file engine pin for the canonical-action-form" lands BEFORE the endpoint-pinned twin.** BE-0297 pins admin.break_glass as a single engine matrix today. BE-0300 (DELETE /v1/admin/break-glass/{session_id}) is the same action constant but a distinct WIRE ENDPOINT — when that lands, the BE-0288 template applies: a sibling file admin_break_glass_end_endpoint_policy_test.go with canonical ids canonicalAdminBreakGlassEndProjectID / canonicalAdminBreakGlassEndSiblingID, parallel structurally but state-independent, framed as "the engine contract specifically for the session-termination verb where an asymmetric regression that left session-creation intact but downgraded session-termination capability cannot ship without flipping one of these expectations". The action-level pin in THIS file remains in place; the duplication is the point.
