ralph/progress.txt:30044:  - The redactor-survival self-check at the head of TestBreakGlassCoversCallSites is load-bearing: without it, an over-aggressive redactor regression would silently false-positive every accept row's marker-survival assertion. Probe the redactor against the marker before walking the table.
ralph/progress.txt:30045:  - The `-run TestBreakGlass` filter matches as a substring, so it widens to include `TestStartBreakGlass*`, `TestBuildSessionToCreate*` is NOT caught (different prefix) but `TestNewBreakGlassServiceRejectsNilDependencies` and `TestStartBreakGlassAuditMetadataElevatedAccess` are — confirmed all green.
ralph/progress.txt:30073:  - When the chokepoint is a package-level pure function (no receiver), the contention burst SHARES NO INSTANCE — every goroutine calls the package symbol directly. The burst's value is the assertion that the package has no shared state. This is different from BE-0395..BE-0398 (shared chokepoint instance with documented mutable state) and from BE-0404 (shared *BreakGlassService).
ralph/progress.txt:30250:  - The canonical pair for a public-method chokepoint (Render is a public method on *Renderer) lives in `package dokploy_test`, not `package dokploy` — mirroring BE-0406's `package migrateimport_test` convention for `Importer.Plan`. The BE-0404 break-glass pair lives in `package store` (not `package store_test`) only because the validator there is package-internal. The rule is: canonical pair package matches the chokepoint's visibility — public method → `pkg_test`, internal helper → `pkg`.
ralph/progress.txt:33454:  - The idempotency_keys CHECK constraint `idempotency_keys_completion_consistent` is the load-bearing reason the byte-identity comparator MUST switch on nil-ness FIRST and dereference value SECOND. A naive field-equality loop would silently round-trip a regression that flipped a pending row's NULL completion columns to zero-value scalars (response_status=0, response_body=[]byte{}, completed_at=epoch) — the schema would reject this on INSERT but the test would not catch it on a peer-row drift. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation file whose row carries nullable completion columns: job_attempts (nullable error_summary / finished_at / result), quota_reservations (nullable released_at / job_id), break_glass_sessions (nullable revoked_at).
